// A row/object field's value can match the setter's top-level shape (a rows
// setter given rows, an object setter given an object block) while still
// being wrong one level deeper — a list of strings where the setter expects
// a list of objects. Matching the field *name* against a setter says nothing
// about whether what's inside it is shaped correctly; this used to compile
// clean and render blank cells with zero signal. This should warn, naming
// the exact field, line, and expected shape — and still emit the value as
// written rather than dropping it. A correctly-shaped row alongside it must
// stay silent: this isn't "nested values are suspicious", only genuine
// shape mismatches.
doc "Nested Shape Mismatch" type=techDoc

section api {
  table entityDetails {
    tableName: "Table" w1
  }
  rows entityDetails [
    {
      tableName: "users",
      columns: [ "id: uuid, PK", "email: string, unique" ]
    },
    {
      tableName: "sessions",
      columns: [ { column: "id", type: "uuid", constraints: "PK", description: "Session id" } ]
    }
  ]
}
